WEBVTT

00:00:09,300 --> 00:00:14,260
What do you think about intravenous vitamin C and baking soda intravenously?

00:00:14,900 --> 00:00:19,540
We found a clinic in Arizona that does that for cancer.

00:00:20,580 --> 00:00:26,900
Intervenous vitamin C, yes, baking soda intravenous, I don't know about that. No.

00:00:26,900 --> 00:00:31,700
You have to see, understand, you have a buffering system in your body.

00:00:31,700 --> 00:00:36,340
You know people that, oh, I just need to alkalize myself. I just need to alkalize myself.

00:00:36,340 --> 00:00:41,380
I just need to get out, you know, but yeah, no, it doesn't work that way.

00:00:41,380 --> 00:00:51,300
If your blood varies very much off of, I think, the pH of 7.345 or something like that for blood,

00:00:52,100 --> 00:00:58,980
you'll die. So your body will buffer it. So if you could somehow alkalize your blood,

00:00:59,540 --> 00:01:05,380
your body would have to be working very hard to acidify it, to balance out the pH,

00:01:05,380 --> 00:01:14,820
or you'll just die. So no, vitamin C, IV, yes, that could be a very good benefit for cancer.

00:01:14,820 --> 00:01:19,780
You could do intravenous vitamin C, you know, you don't have to go away to a clinic,

00:01:19,780 --> 00:01:27,140
just every large city has IV centers that you could do a vitamin C, IV locally.

00:01:27,140 --> 00:01:31,460
Plus you need to do that on a very regular basis once or twice a week for it to be effective.

